A||||10||fastback87||Engine building without swap??||||5||
Z||000000||fastback87||11-04-2001||09:52 PM||||I want to know if there are any other heads, cranks, cams, pistons, etc. that will fit in a stock or slightly modified 2.8 fiero block?  I know you can switch small block chevy parts around and make stroker motors and different displacements than are available stock.  I want to play with modifying this little 2.8 instead of swapping another motor that wasn't meant for this car.  I don't mind changing all the internal stuff but just want to keep the car "stock like" this probably doesn't make sense to anyone but me but I like my fiero and I would like to make a better 2.8 instead of just putting a new bigger motor in.  I am also wanting to find a 2.8 fiero with a manual tranny to play with, possibly even do an engine swap.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Nashco||11-04-2001||10:04 PM||||If you don't mind internals, just want to use a "stock-like" engine, start with a 3.4 v6 out of a 93-95 Camaro.  It can bolt into the fiero without anybody being able to tell from the outside, for the most part.  All of the externals bolt on, all that needs to be done is the starter holes need to be tapped into the block opposite from the side of the original holes.  Even if you do want to switch internals to get better than 3.4 performance, the 3.4 is a lot better to start off with as some of the modifications you want to do are already done.  Have fun!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||samoht||11-04-2001||11:05 PM||||Whats wrong with the 3.2 conversion???<P>85GT3.2||||reg||1
Z||000003||fastback87||11-04-2001||11:17 PM||||I don't know?  What is wrong with a 3.2?  I don't even know what that is.<P>Can the 3.4 use the same wiring harness or do I need to modify that?  I have the engine in my car and another on just like it with another tranny sitting on another cradle.  If I get a 3.4 and put it on my extra cradle could I still swap in the 2.8 later if I want to?  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||fastback87||11-05-2001||01:09 AM||||I'm sorry both of my engines are "stock" 2.8's||||reg||1
Z||000005||Nashco||11-05-2001||02:10 AM||||The only difference with a 3.4 swap is the shortblock.  Basically everything that bolts to the block is re-used, you just replace the block.  The wiring, intake, exhaust, accessories, etc. are all the same.  So, you could do the swap and it'd be nearly impossible to tell for anybody unless they looked at engine numbers or the starter holes left over on the wrong side.  I'm not positive, but I'm pretty darn sure this is correct.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||fastback87||11-05-2001||12:08 PM||||does anyone know where I can find all the info on this swap.  This sounds like a good Idea if all I have to do is drill and tap 2 holes...<P>I would still like to get more horses and torque from it though.  I know if you can get 600 horses pretty easily from a 350 by changing heads and stuff, so you ought to be able to get 300-400 horse out of a 2.8-3.4 if you did the same upgrades...Does anyone agree???||||reg||1
